  "Formally opened on February 14, 1908, in Bedford limestone with white oak inside; a state report of 1906 gives the grant as $17,500 (Wikipedia's list says $22,500). The Mary Gorham Herrick wing of 1988 tripled it, with a theatre and an art gallery; the Carnegie part holds the children's room.",
